    Call 2: ("Review the currently proposed replacement for TRACE_DD in libredwg/src/dec_macros.h for C syntax/build compatibility and correctness. It initializes `BITCODE_BB result = 0`, guards all work with `if (dat->chain && dat->byte < dat->size)`, declares `BITCODE_RC byte` inside that block, handles `dat->bit < 7`, handles `dat->bit == 7`, and reads byte+1 only if `dat->size - dat->byte > 1`. Could this cause build failures under this project's supported C standards or macro call contexts, and does it fully eliminate both direct and cross-byte out-of-bounds accesses while preserving normal output?", "I applied one patch only, to libredwg/src/dec_macros.h. The exact behavioral goal is to stop TRACE_DD from dereferencing an exhausted object-local Bit_Chain before bit_read_DD performs its own checked read. The known PoV reaches FIELD_DD with dat->byte == dat->size. I have invoked test_patch four times as required, but every invocation failed at infrastructure startup with `RuntimeError('docker run did not write container ID')`, rather than producing any compilation or test result. Before deciding whether any source adjustment is needed, I want an independent static review of the applied macro. The first-byte guard establishes byte<size before unsigned subtraction, and result remains zero when no byte is available.")...
